  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Storms have shifted offshore and no longer pose\nany immediate threat to land. Convective Inhibition has set up \nover much of ENC, and this keeps any additional storm formation\nunlikely over land. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Guidance continues to suggest tomorrow will be \nprimarily dry with only an isolated shower or storm possible on \narea breezes in the afternoon. On Wednesday, surface flow \nbecomes more onshore kicking off a period of increasing moisture\nand instability across the Southeast U.S. coastline with a \nmodest uptick of shower and thunderstorm coverage. Another wave \nof low pressure is forecast to lift along the offshore frontal \nboundary Thursday into Friday, pulling it back towards the coast\nand providing a better focal point for more widespread coverage\nof showers and storms into the weekend.",
